      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A limited modding API would be great for all sorts of 3rd party software. \n\nWe already go access to change avatars using OSC, does that mean it will be expanded in the future? \n\nFor a start we could get access to the client settings but I think there is a lot more potential to expand it to a real modding api. \n\nSince we lost the ability to mod the client we lost a bunch of handy tool but with access to a \"limited\" modding api the community could bring a bunch of those tools back. \n\nIn my opinion this would be a grate change that could benefit everyone because the community would come up with great tools for specific use cases that Vrchat can't support like accessibility needs or specific tools that only a select few would care about.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
